==English==
[[Image:Tsetse_head-proboscis.jpeg|thumb|Head of a '''tsetse'''.]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|tzetze}}, {{l|en|tsetze}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|tn|tsêtsê}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/tsitsi/|/sitsi/|/titsi/}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/tsɛtsi/|/sɛtsi/|/tɛtsi/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tsetse.wav|Audio (Berkshire, UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|tsetse}}

# Any [[fly]] of the [[genus]] ''[[Glossina]]'', native to [[Africa]], that feeds on human and animal blood; known primarily as a carrier of parasitic [[trypanosome]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=Stephen G. A. Leak|title=[https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=J1latecW1BQC&lpg=PR16&dq=tsetse&pg=PP1#v=onepage&q&f=false Tsetse Biology and Ecology: Their Role in the Epidemiology and Control of Trypanosomosis]|publisher=CABI Publishing|page=7|passage=Species of ''Trypanosoma'' transmitted by '''tsetse''' cause diseases of economic importance in humans and domestic animals in sub-Saharan Africa.}}

====Usage notes====
* Particularly in North American English, this insect is most commonly referred to as a "tsetse fly." Note: This is also the most common usage in Zimbabwe.

